WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.399
Moving hand-written

00:00:01.211 --> 00:00:02.331
PTX back to

00:00:02.142 --> 00:00:03.899
MLIR in glm-vx

00:00:03.711 --> 00:00:04.878
GPU kernels

00:00:05.406 --> 00:00:06.762
The glm-vx team

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.670
replaced most of

00:00:07.481 --> 00:00:09.238
99 inline PTX

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.028
snippets in their

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.420
GLM inference kernels

00:00:11.314 --> 00:00:12.552
with MLIR NVVM

00:00:12.375 --> 00:00:12.906
ops

00:00:13.047 --> 00:00:14.120
pinning each kernel's

00:00:13.932 --> 00:00:15.288
instructions in tests

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:16.349
to catch regressions

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:17.978
After the switch

00:00:18.096 --> 00:00:19.252
14 of 20

00:00:19.063 --> 00:00:20.195
pinned kernels kept

00:00:20.078 --> 00:00:21.457
every instruction and

00:00:21.269 --> 00:00:22.436
6 got fewer

00:00:22.377 --> 00:00:23.568
because the compiler

00:00:23.379 --> 00:00:24.039
could see the

00:00:23.851 --> 00:00:24.877
surrounding code

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.186
no kernel needs

00:00:25.997 --> 00:00:27.565
more registers and

00:00:27.412 --> 00:00:28.544
one spill dropped

00:00:28.356 --> 00:00:29.287
from 40 to

00:00:29.099 --> 00:00:30.018
8 bytes

00:00:30.542 --> 00:00:31.579
Its kernels had

00:00:31.391 --> 00:00:32.735
99 pieces of

00:00:32.547 --> 00:00:34.126
hand-written PTX in

00:00:33.938 --> 00:00:35.424
25 source files

00:00:35.958 --> 00:00:36.972
Full story on

00:00:36.783 --> 00:00:37.679
the dashboard
